T* () Tj
T* (Title: The Joint Effect of Prompt Specificity and Inference Hyperparameters on Stereotype) Tj
T* (Generation in Open-Source Large Language Models) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Authors: Zerihun Ayele Chala \(corresponding\), Beakal Gizachew Assefa, Elefelious Getachew) Tj
T* (Belay, Tensae Aschalew Andualem) Tj
T* (Affiliation: School of IT and Engineering, Addis Ababa University) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (We thank the Program Committee and Reviewer 1 for the constructive comments. Below we respond) Tj
T* (to each major comment and note where the camera-ready paper was revised.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Comment 1. Only three relatively small models are considered; the narrow selection limits the) Tj
T* (generalizability of the findings and should be broadened or justified.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Response: We agree that restricting the study to mid-size models limits generalizability. We) Tj
T* (retain the three open instruction-tuned models \(Llama 3.1 8B, Mistral 7B, Qwen 2.5 7B\) because) Tj
T* (the treatment of interest is temperature and top-p, which must be set and verified directly at) Tj
T* (generation time. Closed APIs often hide or limit those settings. Keeping models in the 7B-8B) Tj
T* (range also made the full factorial design feasible \(prompt tiers, four decoding conditions,) Tj
T* (three seeds, four demographic dimensions\). In the camera-ready paper we justify this choice in) Tj
T* (Model Selection and state clearly in Limitations that the findings are scoped to mid-size open) Tj
T* (models and may not hold for larger open models or proprietary systems. Extending the design to) Tj
T* (larger models is left as future work.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Comment 2. The rationale for the chosen parameter settings, such as temperature, is not) Tj
T* (explained and should be stated.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Response: We agree and have expanded the Hyperparameter Conditions section. The four settings) Tj
T* (were chosen to cover low and high randomness without a full temperature x top-p grid:) Tj
T* (- T=0.3, top-p=1.0: near-deterministic sampling) Tj
T* (- T=1.0, top-p=0.3: narrow token pool) Tj
T* (- T=1.0, top-p=0.9: common open-ended setting) Tj
T* (- T=1.5, top-p=1.0: higher chance of low-probability tokens) Tj
T* (The camera-ready text states this rationale explicitly and retains the condition table. A) Tj
T* (separate gender temperature supplement remains a sensitivity analysis only.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Comment 3. The conclusion emphasizes that prompt design and model choice matter more than) Tj
T* (hyperparameters, but this claim requires stronger evidence than the current results provide.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Response: We agree. The original comparative ranking overstated what the primary tests support.) Tj
T* (The camera-ready paper states that the primary hypothesis \(tier-by-condition interaction\) was) Tj
T* (not supported. We removed absolute ranking language from the abstract, discussion, and) Tj
T* (conclusion. Prompt-tier and model differences are reported as descriptive results within this) Tj
T* (study, not as a general claim that they always matter more than hyperparameters.) Tj
T* () Tj
